<title>GERMANY: German cocoa imports down at 157,737 T in Jan-July.</title>
<headline>German cocoa imports down at 157,737 T in Jan-July.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German January-July 1996 cocoa bean imports from third countries totalled 157,737 tonnes compared with 161,650 in January-July 1995, federal statistics office data showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Leading suppliers in the seven months included Ivory Coast with 87,083 tonnes, Ghana with 24,618, Indonesia 17,553 and Nigeria with 10,043, excluding beans for toll grinding.</p>
<p>Imports in July were just 22,701 tonnes after 46,434 a year earlier and compared with June imports of 19,115 tonnes.</p>
<p>July import value was 52.39 million marks against 101.38 million a year earlier. --Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
